Subject: [PATCH] clk: qcom: nsscc-ipq5332: match DT RX/TX input order

The IPQ5332 NSSCC binding and the DTS describe the UNIPHY inputs
RX first, TX second, but the driver's DT input indices use the
opposite order. As parent_data uses positional indices, port RX
RCGs have the TX provider in the common clock framework and vice
versa.

Match the binding. Do not change the hardware mux selector mapping
or frequency tables. Both provider rates currently depend on the
same PCS interface so this correction alone need not change the
programmed frequency; its impact on observed link flaps is unknown.

diff --git a/drivers/clk/qcom/nsscc-ipq5332.c b/drivers/clk/qcom/nsscc-ipq5332.c
--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/nsscc-ipq5332.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/nsscc-ipq5332.c
@@ -30,10 +30,10 @@
 	DT_CMN_PLL_NSS_CLK_200M,
 	DT_CMN_PLL_NSS_CLK_300M,
 	DT_GCC_GPLL0_OUT_AUX,
+	DT_UNIPHY0_NSS_RX_CLK,
 	DT_UNIPHY0_NSS_TX_CLK,
-	DT_UNIPHY0_NSS_RX_CLK,
+	DT_UNIPHY1_NSS_RX_CLK,
 	DT_UNIPHY1_NSS_TX_CLK,
-	DT_UNIPHY1_NSS_RX_CLK,
 	DT_XO,
 };
 
